-# locals: set_id (String), sentinel (Sentinel|nil), groups (Array<[id, name]>)
-#
-# The Set edit page's Sentinel tab: authors this Set's Sentinel — the Works'
-# visibility, their group grants and their derivative access — and,
-# separately, sweeps it across the Works the Set holds now. See docs/sets.md.
-#
-# The heading plate, the Save footer and the Apply button are wells, as on the
-# Collection's Sentinel tab; the three parts of the form and the Apply
-# explainer are bare sections split by dividers. Each part opens on "leave as
-# it is", so saving a policy that names one part changes only that part.
- access = sentinel&.work_access || {}
- grants_mode = sentinel&.grants.nil? ? 'keep' : 'replace'
- derivatives_mode = sentinel&.derivatives_enabled ? 'set' : 'keep'
.edit-pane
  .well.p-3.mb-3.rounded-3
    %h5.mb-0 Sentinel
    %p.small.text-muted.mt-3.mb-0
      Choose what every work in this set should allow, save it, then apply it. Each part you leave
      as it is stays as each work has it. Nothing changes until you apply.

  = bootstrap_form_tag(url: sentinel_set_path(set_id), method: :patch) do |f|
    %fieldset
      %legend.h6.mb-1 Visibility
      %p.small.text-subtle.mb-2
        A work can only be public if the collection it is in is public. Works in a restricted
        collection are listed in the report and keep their visibility.
      - [['', 'Leave each work’s visibility as it is'], ['public', 'Make every work public'], ['private', 'Make every work private']].each do |value, label|
        .form-check
          %input.form-check-input{ type: 'radio', id: "work-visibility-#{value.presence || 'keep'}", name: 'work_access[visibility]', value: value, checked: access['visibility'].to_s == value }
          %label.form-check-label{ for: "work-visibility-#{value.presence || 'keep'}" }= label

    %hr.section-divider.my-3

    %div{ data: { controller: 'reveal', 'reveal-when-value': 'replace' } }
      %fieldset
        %legend.h6.mb-1 Groups
        %p.small.text-subtle.mb-2
          Replacing removes every group grant a work has and gives it only the groups below. An empty
          list removes them all. Repository staff keep their access either way.
        .form-check
          %input#work-grants-keep.form-check-input{ type: 'radio', name: 'work_access[grants_mode]', value: 'keep', checked: grants_mode == 'keep', data: { action: 'change->reveal#sync' } }
          %label.form-check-label{ for: 'work-grants-keep' } Keep each work’s groups
        .form-check
          %input#work-grants-replace.form-check-input{ type: 'radio', name: 'work_access[grants_mode]', value: 'replace', checked: grants_mode == 'replace', data: { action: 'change->reveal#sync' } }
          %label.form-check-label{ for: 'work-grants-replace' } Replace each work’s groups with these
      .mt-3{ hidden: grants_mode != 'replace', data: { 'reveal-target': 'section', controller: 'group-permissions', 'group-permissions-resource-value': 'work_access' } }
        = render 'shared/group_permissions', resource: 'work_access', noun: 'work', heading: nil,
                                             grants: sentinel_grant_rows(sentinel, groups), groups: groups

    %hr.section-divider.my-3

    %div{ data: { controller: 'reveal', 'reveal-when-value': 'set' } }
      %fieldset
        %legend.h6.mb-1 Derivative access
        %p.small.text-subtle.mb-2
          Restrict which groups can download each type of file. A file you don't restrict keeps the
          permissions of its work. For images, larger versions must be at least as restricted as
          smaller ones.
        .form-check
          %input#derivatives-keep.form-check-input{ type: 'radio', name: 'sentinel[derivatives_mode]', value: 'keep', checked: derivatives_mode == 'keep', data: { action: 'change->reveal#sync' } }
          %label.form-check-label{ for: 'derivatives-keep' } Leave each work’s derivative access as it is
        .form-check
          %input#derivatives-set.form-check-input{ type: 'radio', name: 'sentinel[derivatives_mode]', value: 'set', checked: derivatives_mode == 'set', data: { action: 'change->reveal#sync' } }
          %label.form-check-label{ for: 'derivatives-set' } Set every work’s derivative access to this policy
      %section.mt-3{ hidden: derivatives_mode != 'set', data: { 'reveal-target': 'section', controller: 'derivative-policy', 'derivative-policy-groups-value': derivative_group_registry(groups) } }
        %h6.derivative-group-heading Images
        %ol.derivative-ladder.list-unstyled.mb-4
          - Sentinel::IMAGE_LADDER.each do |tier|
            = render 'shared/derivative_tier', tier: tier, sentinel: sentinel, groups: groups, open_label: 'Inherit from the work'
        %h6.derivative-group-heading Audio, video and PDF
        %ul.derivative-independent.list-unstyled.mb-0
          - Sentinel::INDEPENDENT.each do |tier|
            = render 'shared/derivative_tier', tier: tier, sentinel: sentinel, groups: groups, open_label: 'Inherit from the work'

    .well.p-3.my-3.rounded-3
      = f.button 'Save', type: :submit, class: 'btn btn-success'
      = link_to 'Cancel', set_path(set_id), class: 'btn btn-warning'

  -# The count is the lazily-loaded frame the My Sets index already uses, so the
  -# number of works is on the screen before Apply is pressed without the edit
  -# page paying a recipe resolution on every load.
  %hr.section-divider.my-3

  %section
    %h5.mb-3 Apply to this set's works
    .d-flex.align-items-baseline.gap-2.mb-2
      %h6.mb-0 This set currently holds
      = turbo_frame_tag "set-works-count-#{set_id}", src: works_count_set_path(set_id), loading: :lazy do
        %span.text-muted Counting…
    %p.small.text-subtle.mb-3
      Applying covers the works the set holds right now, including those it reaches through an
      included collection. Works you have hidden are not touched. You'll get a message when it
      finishes.
    - if sentinel.nil?
      %p.small.text-subtle.mb-0
        %i.fa-solid.fa-circle-info.me-1{ 'aria-hidden' => 'true' }
        Save the Sentinel first.
    - else
      - summary = sentinel_apply_summary(sentinel)
      - if summary.empty?
        %p.small.text-subtle.mb-0
          %i.fa-solid.fa-circle-info.me-1{ 'aria-hidden' => 'true' }
          The saved Sentinel leaves every part as it is, so applying it would change nothing.
      - else
        %h6.mt-4.mb-2 Applying the saved Sentinel will change this:
        %ul.small.mb-3
          - summary.each do |line|
            %li= line
        -# The warning sits before the control it applies to, and only for a
        -# widening: that is the change that discloses material to the public.
        - if sentinel_widens?(sentinel)
          .alert.alert-warning.py-2.px-3.small.d-flex.align-items-start.mb-3{ role: 'alert' }
            %i.fa-solid.fa-triangle-exclamation.me-2.mt-1{ 'aria-hidden' => 'true' }
            %div
              %strong.d-block This makes material public
              Anyone will be able to see these works. Check the set's contents before you apply. The
              admin ledger keeps each work's earlier access, so a developer can restore it.
        .well.p-3.my-3.rounded-3
          = button_to apply_sentinel_set_path(set_id), form: { class: 'd-inline' },
                      class: "btn #{sentinel_widens?(sentinel) ? 'btn-danger' : 'btn-primary'}",
                      data: { turbo_confirm: "Apply this Sentinel to every work in this set? #{summary.join(' ')}",
                              turbo_confirm_title: 'Confirm apply',
                              turbo_confirm_button: 'Apply',
                              turbo_confirm_variant: sentinel_widens?(sentinel) ? 'danger' : 'primary' } do
            Apply to this set's works
